# `.gitignore` keeps local artifacts out of Git. The image build needs an even
# narrower boundary: start with an empty context and admit only Dockerfile inputs.
# Keep this allowlist synchronized with every local path used by COPY.
**


### Docker

!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore


### Python project

# Dependency metadata; README.md is referenced by pyproject.toml.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md

# Importable application package installed by uv and copied into the runtime image.
!app/
!app/**


### PostgreSQL migrations

# Alembic is part of the runtime image, including an initially empty versions directory.
!alembic.ini
!alembic/
!alembic/**


### Generated and local files

# The allowlist opens whole source trees, so mirror the relevant .gitignore rules within them.

# Python bytecode and build products
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so
**/build/
**/dist/
**/*.egg-info/

# Test, coverage, linter, and type-checker state
**/.cache/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.nox/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.pyre/
**/.pytype/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.tox/

# Local environments, logs, and secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.venv/
**/env/
**/venv/
**/ENV/
**/env.bak/
**/venv.bak/
**/.local-secrets/
**/*.log

# Repository, editor, and agent state
**/.git/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/.agents/
**/.codex/
**/.claude/

# OS metadata
**/.DS_Store
